  "schema": "transfer-nullifier-batch-endpoint-v1",
  "scope": "Functional public nullifier-batch source-order and exact single object-write proof only. Existing finite SCT and genuine delivery controls are separate evidence; new genuine delayed/queue controls remain unrun. No new native or negative-control execution credit, no atomic evidence refresh or full Transfer certification. Successful actual modeled inspection derives the source-ordered checks, capacity bound, ordered append, and observed unspent flags/current pending freshness for every input using the qualified complete vector recurrence. Nonempty public success derives exactly one pending-object cache write and frames verifiable/NV/events and all other object keys. Errors preserve the supplied input cache, including possible earlier raw effects; this is not whole-handler rollback. Saturating capacity implies natural sum capacity only with explicit capacity<wordMax. Pending getter/encoding, source-id, word size, nullifier equality, Rust collections/cache ownership and individually authenticated status remain named interfaces. Original elaboration failure is zero credit.",
